es of  personal  liberty and limited government what we  need today using the title of  hillsdale's  matthew spalding's best seller is for us  to loudly and pro  and proudly proclaim yes we still  hold these truths to be self-evident  a return to first principles first  congress must reaffirm the primacy  of congressional authority in article 1  of the constitution  congress must end the practice of  delegating law making authority to  unelected  unaccountable agency government no more  passing vague laws that direct agencies  to fill  in the blanks with specifics  according to their discretion the reins  act  which has passed the house would  introduce both constitutionality  and accountability into the system by  requiring  congress not the bureaucracy but  congress to approve  all major new regulations the act is  simple  the act is profound the act is  revolutionary and its ultimate passage  into law must be  a major priority of the conservative  movement  secondly members of congress must take  back from the fourth branch of  government the power  of the purse granted in sections eight  nine of article one of the constitution  if you grab a bureaucracy by its budget  its heart in mind very well  will soon follow thirdly congress must  rediscover and reinvigorate the 10th  amendment in order to reinstitute  federalism  one of the cornerstones of our  constitutional system  as most here are familiar madison wrote  in federalist 45 the powers delegated to  the federal  government are few and defined those  which are to remain in state governments  are numerous  and indefinite finally  we must celebrate celebrate the role  of risk-taking as an american right  as an american heritage and as an  american  destiny we must educate our fellow  citizens that when we entrust government  agencies to manage our  risk we risk we risk  losing both our freedom and our  prosperity  now all this will require strong and  dedicated  consistent cheerful leadership in  washington  a